# packages/plugin-sdk — Plugin SDK

Owners: Platform team (identity: @nexora/platform)

Scope: the canonical SDK for building every first-party and third-party
Nexora plugin (SAD.md §7). First-party apps are plugins too (ADR-003), so
this package is the single installability contract for the platform.

Rules:
- NO business logic. The SDK is generic and domain-agnostic.
- Dependencies are limited to: @nexora/contracts, @nexora/shared,
  @nexora/config, @nexora/agent-sdk. Do not add others.
- NO coupling to React, Next.js, HTTP frameworks, Node APIs, databases,
  or LLM providers. Frontend surfaces are declarative (component ids),
  never framework code.
- Reuse the canonical contracts and shared utilities; never duplicate them.
- The plugin manifest is the canonical `PluginManifest` from
  @nexora/contracts/plugin — the SDK extends, never redefines it.
- Contract changes require a compatibility review.
